.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Superposing a uniform stream of speed U_\infty with a doublet of strength \kappa = 2\pi U_\infty R^2 places a circular streamline of radius R exactly at the origin -- a solid cylinder, in potential-flow terms. Adding a point vortex of circulation \Gamma at the same location keeps that circle intact (a vortex centered on the circle induces purely tangential velocity there) while breaking its front-back symmetry, generating lift with no viscosity anywhere in the calculation. This example builds that flow with flow_past_cylinder, plots its surface pressure coefficient">

